Section: hamradio
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/packet-net/pdn-ax25-tools
Description: run a program for inbound AX.25 calls
 Answers inbound AX.25 calls. Each call either runs a program with the session
 on its standard input and output, or is forwarded to a local TCP service, so
 writing a packet service becomes writing a program that reads stdin. This is
 what ax25d did, without the kernel stack it depended on.
 .
 The callsign called is the whole address and so the whole routing decision;
 there are no port numbers on the AX.25 side. The calling station is passed to
 the program as %r in its arguments and as AX25_CALLER in its environment.
 .
 Carries its own AX.25 v2.2 data link and speaks KISS to a TNC over a serial
 port or over TCP, so it needs no kernel support, no kissattach and no
 privilege. It declines to run as root, because it runs programs on behalf of
 whoever calls in and cannot drop privileges first.
 .
 Self-contained: bundles its own .NET runtime, so no system runtime is
 required.

